    "Across 5 fast-opcode traces in the same-invocation opt-level=3 paired benchmark, the fast-opcode rewrite consistently reduces HostcallPayloadArena::marshal_with_controls latency by 3.51% (1.036x; 4.23% / 1.044x in the prior pass) with zero hash divergence and -0.19% noise on the non-fast-opcode negative control.",
    "The negative control (tool.custom_generic at ~878 ns) reveals that hostcall_superinstruction_telemetry(Some(opcode)) accounts for ~6 us per call on both arms of marshal_with_controls; further marshalling wins require optimizing superinstruction trace tracking rather than deeper hash-fusion rewrites.",
    "Because fast-opcode fusion is strictly positive with verified hash identity and calibrated conservative pricing (84 vs 100), keeping PI_HOSTCALL_EGRAPH_REWRITE enabled by default with kill-switch override is justified."
